# Release workflow (manual only)

## Permission and safety
- Always ask the user before any release action.
- Never run release steps automatically or without explicit approval.

## The two phases
The release script is the canonical SFX release-script block (`bin/release.sh`, placed
unchanged; its README in the sfx-wp-plugin-skills repository describes it). Its values
live in `bin/plugin.conf` (`KIND=theme`). Never edit `bin/release.sh` by hand: a new
version is placed by `adopt-block`.

1. **Bump** on a clean `main` equal to `origin/main`:
   `bash bin/release.sh patch|minor|major`. It creates `release/<next>`, sets the one
   `Version:` line of `style.css`, moves the `## [Unreleased]` entries of `CHANGELOG.md`
   under the new version, writes `languages/sfxtheme.pot`, runs `bash quality.sh` and
   stops. Review the diff, commit, open a pull request and merge it (`AGENTS.md`
   invariant 7).
2. **Publish** on `main` after that merge: `bash bin/release.sh publish`. It builds
   `sfx-bricks-child-<version>.zip` with `git archive` from `HEAD`, holding only the
   `SHIPPED` entries under `sfx-bricks-child/`, refuses a ZIP that differs from them,
   then pushes the annotated tag `v<version>` and creates the GitHub release.
   `bash bin/release.sh publish --no-upload` stops after the ZIP and prints its path.

A pre-release `X.Y.Z-rc.N` is set and tagged by hand; the script publishes it as a
GitHub pre-release.
